# ==============================================================================
# GazProf Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# This file contains environment variables required for the application.
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your actual values.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit the `.env` file to version control!
# The `.env` file is already excluded via .gitignore.
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# EMAILJS CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================
# EmailJS is used for sending password reset OTP emails to users.
# Sign up and configure at: https://dashboard.emailjs.com/
#
# Setup steps:
# 1. Create an account at https://dashboard.emailjs.com/sign_up
# 2. Add an Email Service (connect your email provider: Outlook, Gmail, etc.)
# 3. Create an Email Template for OTP verification
# 4. Get your User ID from Account > General section
#
# Email Template variables available:
# - {{to_email}} - recipient email address
# - {{otp_code}} - 4-digit OTP code
# - {{message}} - custom message (optional)

EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id_here
# Find this at: EmailJS Dashboard > Email Services > Your Service > Service ID

EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id_here
# Find this at: EmailJS Dashboard > Email Templates > Your Template > Template ID

EMAILJS_USER_ID=your_user_id_here
# Find this at: EmailJS Dashboard > Account > General > User ID (Public Key)

EMAIL=your_email@example.com
# The email address that will send OTP messages
# This should match the email configured in your EmailJS service

EMAIL_PASSWORD=your_email_password
# Password for the email account above
# 
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES:
# - For Outlook/Gmail with 2FA enabled, you MUST use an App Password
# - Outlook: Account > Security > Advanced security options > App passwords
# - Gmail: Account > Security > 2-Step Verification > App passwords
# - Never use your regular email password here if 2FA is enabled

# ==============================================================================
# FIREBASE CLOUD MESSAGING (FCM) CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================
# FCM is used for sending push notifications to drivers when new orders are
# created or when urgent notifications need to be sent.
#
# Setup steps:
# 1. Go to Firebase Console: https://console.firebase.google.com/
# 2. Select your project (or create a new one)
# 3. Go to Project Settings (gear icon) > Service Accounts tab
# 4. Click "Generate new private key" button
# 5. A JSON file will be downloaded (e.g., gazprof-firebase-adminsdk.json)
# 6. Encode the JSON file to base64 using the command below:
#
#    On Linux/macOS:
#    base64 -i gazprof-firebase-adminsdk.json | tr -d '\n' > fcm_key_base64.txt
#
#    On Windows (PowerShell):
#    [Convert]::ToBase64String([IO.File]::ReadAllBytes("gazprof-firebase-adminsdk.json")) | Out-File -Encoding ASCII fcm_key_base64.txt
#
# 7. Copy the entire base64 string (no line breaks) and paste below

FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_BASE64=your_base64_encoded_service_account_key_here
# This is the base64-encoded content of your Firebase service account JSON file
# The string will be very long (1000+ characters) - this is normal
# Make sure there are NO line breaks in the base64 string

# ==============================================================================
# NOTES
# ==============================================================================
# - After creating your `.env` file, make sure it's in .gitignore (it should be)
# - Restart your Flutter app after changing any environment variables
# - For development, you can use test credentials
# - For production, use proper credentials and secure them appropriately
#
# TROUBLESHOOTING:
# - If OTP emails don't send, check EmailJS dashboard for error logs
# - If push notifications don't work, verify FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_BASE64 is correct
# - Make sure all variables are on a single line (no line breaks in values)
# ==============================================================================
